body+='<h2>Meeting outcome and remaining gaps</h2><p>The default scenario is a validated 100 M€ planning option with 0.037 M€ unused base capacity. It selects 162 base Programs plus four PMI Programs; 14 carry-over Programs use partial approved baseline caps. The total IT cost is 575.467463038512 M€.</p><div class="gap"><b>Allocation balances retained:</b> 11.250895735 M€ EW unallocated (the user-approved 22.6303317536% share); 1.357 M€ explicitly unallocated Indirect Cross BU; and 0.465 M€ missing from Bu-06’s source percentages. Total unallocated = 13.072895735 M€. The last two balances require source-owner allocation decisions if leadership wants every euro assigned to a BU. All remain included in the total.</div><p>Source completeness is separate from arithmetic: 446 source Programs become 433 active records after nine missing requests and four invalid decisions are excluded. Scope completeness is 97.09%; 13.08% of funded base Programs cost remains unallocated, including the approved EW balance. These are disclosed source conditions, not silently repaired values. No external handoff or Planisware load is required for this build.</p>'
body+='<h2>Ten validated scenarios</h2>'+table(['Scenario','Base funded','F&R / EW','BU Led','PMI on top','Operations','Total IT','Over budget'],scenarioRows)+'<p>Scenario 07 deliberately demonstrates a 0.413 M€ manual overspend, which remains visible. Scenario 09 uses whole Programs: the F&R 1 M€ reduction request removes 2 M€ of Programs, while BU adds 1 M€; the 100 M€ budget is unchanged. Targets are not fractional automatic funding instructions.</p><p><a href="Ten-scenarios-Programs-trace.csv">All 4,330 scenario Programs records, with source rows and before/after changes</a></p>'+detail
body+='<h2>QA evidence</h2>'+table(['Suite','Passed','Checks','Result'],suite)+'<p>The independent oracle verifies 21,650 row-level values (433 Programs × 10 scenarios × five fields: request, merit, stage, automatic funding and final funding), source-cell extraction, exact recipient allocation, Operations services, and global reconciliation. Browser tests cover six tabs, two viewport sizes, source refresh, edits, persistence, portable import/integrity, finalisation and recovery. Extract coverage: 22 datasets and 649 column filters.</p><p>Finance arithmetic uses full precision; display uses upward one-decimal rounding. The browser was tested in Chrome on Windows. No multi-user server, external submission or organizational approval is claimed.</p>'
body+='<h2>How to reproduce a manual Excel check</h2><ol><li>Use the source workbook SHA-256 values recorded below; exclude BU row 276 from Programs and the 13 audit-excluded records.</li><li>Convert K€ requests/baselines/benefits to M€. Apply the selected scenario request and merit overlays without changing original source cells.</li><li>Classify and rank with the recorded rule engine; confirmed carry funding is min(request, baseline). Select whole requests against each lever and the total budget, then apply logged manual decisions.</li><li>For each funded BU record, multiply by its exact spend allocation fractions. For each EW record, use row 276 fractions × 1,000; preserve Not allocated.</li><li>Add Bill of IT top-level recipient own consumption, Region and Function allocation once. Add PMI separately, without BU charge.</li><li>Reconcile against the Finance Ledger and both allocation summary sheets in each scenario workbook.</li></ol>'
